WEBVTT

1
00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.600
Doctor Durand. It's not safe.
We don't know if it's over.

2
00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.160
She is out there. I have to find her.

3
00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.200
I know where she was during the attack.
I can walk.

4
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.040
- I can't leave her.
- Listen to me.

5
00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.160
If your sister's dead. I'm sorry.

6
00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.160
There's nothing we can do for her.

7
00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:33.280
If she's alive. where do you think she'd go?

8
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.920
She was on her way here...

9
00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.080
You need to be here when she arrives.

10
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.400
Come on.

11
00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.040
I'm talking to you!

12
00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.520
Fred. throw him a bottle.

13
00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:32.880
We don't know if there are other survivors.

14
00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.280
The pulse destroyed all
the electrical circuits above ground.

15
00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:40.080
The equipment we had with us
in the tunnel is okay.

16
00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:44.960
We're rigging the generator.

17
00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:48.600
Well?

18
00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.040
Is there any radio chatter?

19
00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.680
Nothing at all.

20
00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:54.080
All the frequencies are dead.

21
00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.440
Even the emergency band.

22
00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:59.160
Keep searching.

23
00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.400
Where are you going?

24
00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.480
I need to check the array.

25
00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:55.160
The dishes.
The colonel told me I could go.

26
00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:56.800
Okay. go ahead.

27
00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.600
Are you okay?

28
00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:04.080
I keep thinking about my family.

29
00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:41.040
Listen.

30
00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:51.920
Which band is it on?

31
00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.160
Not one of ours.
We don't use this frequency.

32
00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.560
Where's it coming from?

33
00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:04.240
Somewhere northeast of our position.

34
00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.520
I can't be exact.

35
00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:08.880
I've never heard this kind of signal.

36
00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.680
Do you think it's extra-terrestrial?

37
00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:15.280
I don't know.

38
00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:16.320
Maybe they are already here?

39
00:15:19.160 --> 00:15:20.160
Where is Doctor Durand?

40
00:25:37.120 --> 00:25:38.240
What's your name?

41
00:25:42.160 --> 00:25:44.040
Don't be afraid. you can tell me.

42
00:25:44.040 --> 00:25:46.280
I'm Catherine. and you?

43
00:25:49.800 --> 00:25:51.720
Where are your parents?

44
00:25:52.960 --> 00:25:55.720
My dad said we had to run.

45
00:25:55.720 --> 00:25:59.520
And then I hid in a cave.

46
00:25:59.520 --> 00:26:02.600
Now I can't find them.

47
00:26:04.400 --> 00:26:05.760
Where do you live?

48
00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:07.840
In Grenoble.

49
00:26:07.840 --> 00:26:11.440
I'm also going to Grenoble.

50
00:26:11.440 --> 00:26:12.680
Come with me.

51
00:26:12.680 --> 00:26:16.520
We will look for your parents together.

52
00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:23.160
Who is Sophia?

53
00:26:25.200 --> 00:26:27.840
...I heard you.

54
00:26:27.840 --> 00:26:29.720
You were saying. "Sophia. Sophia!"

55
00:26:31.480 --> 00:26:32.800
My sister.

56
00:26:32.800 --> 00:26:34.520
Did you lose her too?

57
00:26:35.600 --> 00:26:36.840
Yes.

58
00:26:36.840 --> 00:26:39.440
Maybe she's with my mum and dad and brother.

59
00:26:41.320 --> 00:26:43.880
Don't worry - they'll look after her as well.

60
00:26:46.520 --> 00:26:48.320
I saw some people who were dead.

61
00:26:50.560 --> 00:26:51.880
Try not to think about that.

62
00:26:55.960 --> 00:26:56.880
Think of something else.

63
00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:01.520
No noise. understand?

64
00:27:04.720 --> 00:27:06.320
What are you doing?

65
00:27:07.400 --> 00:27:09.520
Who's she?

66
00:27:09.520 --> 00:27:12.040
I found her in the forest.
She lost her parents. Let her go.

67
00:27:14.880 --> 00:27:15.760
Don't be scared.

68
00:27:15.760 --> 00:27:17.800
They're friends. they want hurt you.

69
00:27:20.560 --> 00:27:22.560
Why did you leave?

70
00:27:22.560 --> 00:27:23.800
I had to find my sister.

71
00:27:26.160 --> 00:27:27.440
I found her car up there.

72
00:27:28.600 --> 00:27:29.640
But not her.

73
00:27:29.640 --> 00:27:31.640
Perhaps she went back to Grenoble.

74
00:27:31.640 --> 00:27:32.840
I can't let you go.

75
00:27:32.840 --> 00:27:35.440
We don't know what's happening.
There could be another attack.

76
00:27:35.440 --> 00:27:36.960
You don't have to come.

77
00:27:40.880 --> 00:27:42.840
What are you going to do. shoot us?

78
00:27:52.160 --> 00:27:56.960
We'll go but only because we need
to find out what's happening.

79
00:27:56.960 --> 00:27:59.320
From now on. do exactly as I say.

80
00:27:59.320 --> 00:28:03.280
Move when I say. stop when I say.

81
00:28:03.280 --> 00:28:04.400
Is that clear?

82
00:28:09.520 --> 00:28:10.760
Let's go.

83
00:28:10.760 --> 00:28:13.120
Stay alert.

84
00:32:31.120 --> 00:32:32.320
Civilians.

85
00:32:32.320 --> 00:32:33.640
Where?

86
00:32:33.640 --> 00:32:35.680
Close by the supermarket.

87
00:32:41.720 --> 00:32:44.800
She could be with them.

88
00:32:49.560 --> 00:32:52.480
Please.

89
00:32:52.480 --> 00:32:55.040
Okay. let's go.

90
00:34:36.920 --> 00:34:37.800
Where did they all go?

91
00:34:39.040 --> 00:34:40.200
Set up a perimeter.

92
00:35:09.520 --> 00:35:10.480
What is it?

93
00:36:00.160 --> 00:36:01.080
Light!

94
00:36:21.240 --> 00:36:22.760
Damn.

95
00:36:24.720 --> 00:36:26.800
What the fuck?

96
00:36:33.200 --> 00:36:33.960
On the roof!

97
00:36:33.960 --> 00:36:35.640
Something on the roof!

98
00:37:16.240 --> 00:37:18.080
Hold your fire!

99
00:37:18.080 --> 00:37:19.200
Only on sight!

100
00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:21.200
What's up there?

101
00:37:21.200 --> 00:37:22.800
I don't know.

102
00:37:37.760 --> 00:37:38.760
What is it?

103
00:37:40.040 --> 00:37:41.040
No noise.

104
00:37:45.240 --> 00:37:46.240
Cover me!

105
00:37:51.400 --> 00:37:52.840
Put pressure on the wound.

106
00:37:56.800 --> 00:37:57.800
Look after him.

107
00:38:02.440 --> 00:38:04.800
Where are the doctor and the little girl?

108
00:38:39.840 --> 00:38:41.560
What the fuck was that?
Did you see it?

109
00:38:41.560 --> 00:38:43.560
- No.
- You OK?

110
00:38:44.480 --> 00:38:45.440
Are you hurt?

111
00:38:45.440 --> 00:38:46.800
Where's the kid?

112
00:40:36.480 --> 00:40:37.720
Shit. What was that?

113
00:40:38.880 --> 00:40:40.120
I don't know.

114
00:40:40.120 --> 00:40:41.280
They're gone.

115
00:40:54.640 --> 00:40:56.040
Don't look.

116
00:40:58.320 --> 00:41:00.080
I'm sorry.

117
00:41:00.080 --> 00:41:02.360
We've got to go. We can't stay here.
Too dangerous.

118
00:41:07.600 --> 00:41:08.560
We can't leave her.

119
00:41:09.920 --> 00:41:11.160
I've got men on the ground.

120
00:41:11.160 --> 00:41:11.880
I've got no choice.

121
00:44:25.640 --> 00:44:26.600
I'm sorry...

122
00:44:28.800 --> 00:44:30.440
We should never have gone into the town.

123
00:44:31.600 --> 00:44:32.840
I gave the order.

124
00:44:35.680 --> 00:44:39.040
I should've protected her.
I should've done something.

125
00:44:39.040 --> 00:44:40.720
There was nothing you could have done.

126
00:44:45.280 --> 00:44:46.520
Did you see...

127
00:44:49.200 --> 00:44:51.200
...what it was?

128
00:44:53.040 --> 00:44:54.640
No.

129
00:44:56.120 --> 00:44:57.760
But whatever it was. it was waiting for us.

130
00:45:01.200 --> 00:45:02.800
I can't understand.

131
00:45:03.960 --> 00:45:05.320
Why?

132
00:45:08.560 --> 00:45:10.320
Maybe they see us as a threat?

133
00:45:11.800 --> 00:45:13.080
They're scared of a little girl?

134
00:45:13.080 --> 00:45:15.680
Then maybe we have something they want?

135
00:45:17.440 --> 00:45:22.520
There are closer planets with resources.
Water and minerals.

136
00:45:23.800 --> 00:45:25.520
Anything they might need.

137
00:45:28.400 --> 00:45:31.400
It makes no sense.

138
00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:35.200
It makes sense to them.

139
00:45:46.120 --> 00:45:47.280
I'm going to bed.
